From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000092 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: reject graphics pipelines without a vertex shader (STEAMAC-AH)

STEAMAC-AH event ef17b253337c4bedb98fa721faae7bb3 (1.9.13, M4 Pro,
appid 1449560) faults at kk_cmd_bind_shaders+128 with KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS
0xe8, under vk_graphics_pipeline_cmd_bind / vkCmdBindPipeline on the vkr
ring thread. The shipped driver (UUID 632D1882-1FCA-36D6-B695-FAC5EC96A7DB,
matching the event) has `ldr x8, [x26, #0xe8]` there for the vertex stage:
x26 is the vertex kk_shader and 0xe8 its pipeline.gfx.ds_handle, so the
bound graphics pipeline had no vertex shader. KosmicKrisp exposes neither
graphics pipeline libraries nor shader objects, so such a pipeline can only
come from vkCreateGraphicsPipelines without a vertex stage
(VUID-VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo-stage-02096). Which pipeline of the game
did that is not established by the report.

Reject a complete graphics pipeline whose stages have no vertex or mesh
shader before any shader is compiled or looked up in a cache, and log the
stages it was given, its libraries and flags. Venus creates pipelines
asynchronously: virglrenderer keeps a placeholder for the failed pipeline
and drops its draws instead of losing the context, and the next report
names the request.

Repro host/moltenvk/repro/sentry-ah-no-vertex.c (REPRO_CASE=sentry-ah),
Metal API validation on:
- Before (main, 0091): a fragment-shader-only pipeline faults the process
  (SIGSEGV at creation in kk_gather_program).
- After: its creation fails with VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN and a NULL handle, the
  rejection is logged; a vertex + fragment control draws every pixel green.
---
--- a/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/runtime/vk_pipeline.c
@@ -2105,6 +2105,42 @@
       vk_dynamic_graphics_state_fill(&pipeline->linked.dynamic, &state_tmp);
    }
 
+   /* steamac: a complete graphics pipeline must have a vertex (or mesh)
+    * shader (VUID-VkGraphicsPipelineCreateInfo-stage-02096). Created without
+    * one (pStages with only a fragment shader, or a link whose libraries and
+    * own pStages give none), it binds with no vertex shader, and KosmicKrisp
+    * dereferences that at vkCmdBindPipeline (STEAMAC-AH: the VM process
+    * faulted). Fail its creation: Venus creates pipelines asynchronously, so
+    * virglrenderer keeps a placeholder whose draws it drops, and the log
+    * names what the pipeline was given. */
+   if (!is_library) {
+      VkShaderStageFlags linked_stages = 0;
+      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < compile_info.stage_count; i++)
+         linked_stages |= mesa_to_vk_shader_stage(compile_info.stages[i].stage);
+      if (!(linked_stages & (VK_SHADER_STAGE_VERTEX_BIT |
+                             VK_SHADER_STAGE_MESH_BIT_EXT))) {
+         const VkPipelineLibraryCreateInfoKHR *libs_info =
+            vk_find_struct_const(pCreateInfo->pNext,
+                                 PIPELINE_LIBRARY_CREATE_INFO_KHR);
+         const VkGraphicsPipelineLibraryCreateInfoEXT *gpl_info =
+            vk_find_struct_const(pCreateInfo->pNext,
+                                 GRAPHICS_PIPELINE_LIBRARY_CREATE_INFO_EXT);
+         VkShaderStageFlags given_stages = 0;
+         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < pCreateInfo->stageCount; i++)
+            given_stages |= pCreateInfo->pStages[i].stage;
+         mesa_loge("vk: graphics pipeline without a vertex shader rejected: "
+                   "stages 0x%x, pStages 0x%x (%u), libraries %u, "
+                   "library flags %s0x%x, flags 0x%llx",
+                   linked_stages, given_stages, pCreateInfo->stageCount,
+                   libs_info != NULL ? libs_info->libraryCount : 0,
+                   gpl_info != NULL ? "" : "absent ",
+                   gpl_info != NULL ? gpl_info->flags : 0,
+                   (unsigned long long)pipeline_flags);
+         result = vk_error(device, VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN);
+         goto fail_stages;
+      }
+   }
+
    if (bin_info != NULL && bin_info->binaryCount > 0) {
       const uint32_t expected_binary_count = compile_info.retain_precomp ?
          (2 * pCreateInfo->stageCount) : pCreateInfo->stageCount;
-- 
